ConfigEntryDefinition.description:
@ref LLP 0036#declared-configuration-in-the-manifest — one declared config
entry: names, purposes, and acquisition metadata are app source (public by
construction); values never appear in any manifest.

permissionBacking.description:
Durable row-existence projection that grants the room permission in
sessions mode. The subject field equals the connection-bound user id;
every mapped table field equals its named room-scope field.

uses.description:
@ref LLP 0036#declared-configuration-in-the-manifest — D8: the config
entries this function may receive. Declaring an entry makes it exist;
only functions that name it here are granted it at runtime.

description:
Closed `/app/ensure` request family. Explicit variants are attempted first;
because the legacy object also denies unknown fields, the presence of an
invalid or unknown `intent` can never fall back to legacy provisioning.
